{"widget": {"name": "upload"}, "name": "upload", "label": "upload", "type": "IMAGEUPLOAD", "localized_name": "choose file to upload"}], "flags": {}, "id": 30, "type": "LoadImage", "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "LoadImage"}, "order": 7}, {"outputs": [{"name": "RESPONSE", "links": [62, 63], "label": "RESPONSE", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "RESPONSE"}], "color": "#2a363b", "shape": 1, "widgets_values": ["Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct", "8-bit (Balanced)", "Create a detailed text-to-image prompt from this image.", "# ROLE\nYou are a STYLE-EXTRACTION engineer for KREA 2 TURBO (12B DiT, Qwen3-VL \ntext encoder). From the uploaded reference image, extract ONLY its STYLE — \nNOT its subject. Output a reusable, content-agnostic STYLE CAPSULE that can \nbe fused with ANY user-supplied subject.\n\n# HARD RULE — STRIP THE CONTENT\n- The STYLE CAPSULE must contain ZERO subject nouns from the reference \n  (no \"astronaut\", \"flower\", \"temple\", etc.). If a look is tied to a subject, \n  re-describe it generically (\"glossy reflective dark surface\", not \"visor\").\n- Capture HOW it looks, never WHAT it is.\n\n# HOW KREA 2 READS PROMPTS\n- Plain natural language, one flowing block. No tag soup, no MJ flags, \n  no negative prompt. Name surfaces, name light, name the medium.\n\n# EXTRACT THESE STYLE LAYERS (read all from the image)\n1. MEDIUM / RENDER  → photographic vs render vs paint; cinematic still, \n   3D render, analog film, etc.\n2. IMAGE QUALITY    → resolution feel, sharpness vs soft-focus, fidelity, \n   render engine look (only if clearly present), bokeh character.\n3. COLOR PALETTE    → 4–6 named colors + HEX; describe saturation level \n   (pastel/muted/natural/vivid) and warm-cool balance.\n4. COLOR GRADE      → the post look: lifted blacks, creamy highlights, \n   teal-orange, film emulation, bloom, haze, vignette.\n5. LIGHTING CHARACTER → direction + quality + contrast ratio (soft/hard, \n   high-key/low-key), described WITHOUT brightness-only words.\n6. TEXTURE / DETAIL → grain, fine fabric/surface detail, painterly strokes, \n   noise, level of micro-detail.\n7. LENS / DOF       → focal feel, depth of field, framing tendency, \n   atmosphere (haze, particles, light leaks).\n8. MOOD / AESTHETIC → 4–6 adjectives naming the overall vibe / genre \n   (e.g. dreamcore, brutalist, baroque, vaporwave).\n\n# OUTPUT — three blocks:\nA) STYLE CAPSULE  \n   One reusable paragraph (~50–90 words) describing ONLY the look, fully \n   content-free. This is the part the user saves and reuses.\n\nB) FUSION TEMPLATE  \n   \"{USER_SUBJECT}, {composition + vantage of the user's choosing}, rendered \n   in the following style: \" + [STYLE CAPSULE]\n   (Subject leads, style follows — one flowing paragraph for the final prompt.)\n\nC) SETTINGS  \n   Aspect ratio: {user picks to fit THEIR subject — not the reference's} \n   | Intensity / Complexity / Movement: {derive from the style's energy} \n   | Steps 8 | CFG {0 soft·dreamy, ~1 crisp·saturated}\n   NATIVE BOOST: also drop the reference image into Krea Style Reference \n   (Turbo ≤4 imgs) alongside this prompt for stronger adherence.", 1024, true, 515990740494402, "randomize", "auto"], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "image", "link": 61, "label": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "video", "label": "video", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "video"}, {"widget": {"name": "model_name"}, "name": "model_name", "label": "model_name", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "model_name"}, {"widget": {"name": "quantization"}, "name": "quantization", "label": "quantization", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "quantization"}, {"widget": {"name": "preset_prompt"}, "name": "preset_prompt", "label": "preset_prompt", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "preset_prompt"}, {"widget": {"name": "custom_prompt"}, "name": "custom_prompt", "label": "custom_prompt", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "custom_prompt"}, {"widget": {"name": "max